comments.body:
@participant1  Thanks for the query. I tested it, and I got all table names as expected. There is no error in the browser developer console.

If I use the code input, in the network analyzer in the dev tools I can see the query. But in the builder option, there is no query in the dev tools shown.

EDIT: I also checked the datasource settings one more time. In my manually added datasource there are exactly the same settings.

@reporter thanks for the testing.. so the needed data arrives in the browser, but somehow it does not get into that select-box...

a quick question.. do you have maybe some "strange" characters in the table names? spaces? non-enighlish characters?

basically, do the table-names contain anything except the english letters from `a` to `z` and the digits `0` to `9` ?

@participant1 No, sorry for the unclear words. It does not reach the browser. In case of the provisioned datasource in the query builder the browser does not fetch the data. 

The only thing my table names contains in addition to your chars are `A` to `Z`, but no english letters.

In the Code editor I can see all table names.

@participant1 Hi, i can confirm the findings of the @reporter as well. 
If the Datasource is added manually the XHR query call can be detected from the inspector, while if the Datasource has been provisioned via YAML the XHR query call is missing. 

Did anyone find what is missing in the YAML Configuration in order to set this up properly? Or its a bug? @participant4

@participant6 
> So if you provision by file, add the `database` field inside `jsonData`, not outside and it will work.

Thanks for the hint, but in my case this is not working.
